 "briefing": "# Canva Briefing: Changes from 16 October to 15 November 2026\n\n**Meeting date:** 17 November 2026\n**Prepared:** 15 November 2026\n**Window covered:** 16 October to 15 November 2026\n\n## Research Status\n\nNo verified developments for the 30-day window were retrieved. Every search attempt returned a \"Rate limit exceeded\" error, so no news items, product launches, executive or key hires, or deals could be confirmed with a dated, source-linked URL. Under the brief's sourcing rules, no unverified items are included. This section should be treated as a gap, not as evidence that nothing changed.\n\n## News\n\nNo dated news items from the window were verified. Canva's newsroom ([1]) and blog ([2]) are the primary places to check for official announcements, and they should be reviewed before the meeting.\n\n## Product Launches\n\nNo product launches from the window were verified. Launch announcements are usually published first on the newsroom and blog, so these are the first places to check for new features, AI tools, or product line changes.\n\n## Executive and Key Hires\n\nNo executive appointments, departures, promotions, or board changes from the window were verified. Leadership changes are often confirmed first in press releases or by reputable business press, so both should be checked for any appointments since mid-October.\n\n## Deals\n\nNo partnerships, acquisitions, investments, customer agreements, or channel agreements from the window were verified. Deals of this kind are typically covered by major business outlets, which should be searched for Canva-related coverage dated 16 October to 15 November 2026 ([3], [4], [5], [6], [7]).\n\n## Recommended Verification Before the Meeting\n\nBefore 17 November, the following checks should be completed and filtered to the window:\n\n- **Official channels:** Canva newsroom ([1]) and blog ([2]) for press releases and product announcements.\n- **Corroboration:** Reuters ([3]), Bloomberg ([4]), TechCrunch ([5]), The Information ([6]), and the Financial Times ([7]) for news, hires, and deals.\n- **Filing and social checks:** Canva's official social accounts and any regulatory filings, if they apply to a deal or investment.\n\nAny item found should be logged with its publication date and a direct URL before it is used in the briefing.\n\n## Open Questions for the Meeting\n\n1. Which news items, product launches, or leadership changes from the past 30 days should we treat as most significant, and where were they first published?\n2. Have any partnerships, acquisitions, investments, or customer or channel agreements been signed since mid-October 2026, and do any of them change how Canva would work with us?\n3. Which new products or features launched in the past month are being rolled out to our customer segment, and what timelines and support arrangements apply?\n\n### Sources\n\n[1] Canva Newsroom: https://www.canva.com/newsroom/\n[2] Canva Blog: https://www.canva.com/blog/\n[3] Reuters: https://www.reuters.com\n[4] Bloomberg: https://www.bloomberg.com\n[5] TechCrunch: https://techcrunch.com\n[6] The Information: https://www.theinformation.com\n[7] Financial Times: https://www.ft.com",
